# Universe content · life · extinct life
# researched: LibreTexts Historical Geology "The Big Five"; US National Park Service "Mass Extinctions Through
#   Geologic Time"; Open Geology "Mass extinctions"; Smithsonian and Discover Wildlife prehistoric-animal features;
#   standard paleontology for dinosaur groups, sea reptiles, megafauna and extinct plants
# Extinct life seeds what evolution can produce, and stays greyed out on the Tree of Life forever.
# Spec: docs/CONTENT-FORMAT.md · wiki/systems/r08-life-sim.md · docs/wiki/stages-of-life.md

# ── Mass extinctions (the Big Five, and after) ──

@extinction end-ordovician
name: End-Ordovician extinction
real: yes
when-mya: 445
lost: about 85% of species, all in the seas (land wasn't settled yet)

@extinction late-devonian
name: Late Devonian extinction
real: yes
when-mya: 372..359
lost: reefs and many fish, over a long stretch

@extinction end-permian
name: End-Permian extinction ("the Great Dying")
real: yes
when-mya: 252
lost: about 90% of species, including the last trilobites

@extinction end-triassic
name: End-Triassic extinction
real: yes
when-mya: 201
lost: about 75% of species; driven by global warming; cleared the way for dinosaurs

@extinction end-cretaceous
name: End-Cretaceous extinction
real: yes
when-mya: 66
cause: an asteroid impact
lost: all non-bird dinosaurs, ammonites, plesiosaurs and mosasaurs; mammals took over after

@extinction human-era
name: Human-era extinction
real: yes
says: a sixth mass extinction may be under way, driven by one thinking species

# ── The first strange animals ──

@extinct dickinsonia
name: Dickinsonia
real: yes
when-mya: about 560
says: a flat, frilly, rug-like early animal over a meter wide (Ediacaran life)

@extinct ediacaran-life
name: Ediacaran life
real: yes
says: soft quilted creatures from before the Cambrian, unlike anything alive now

@extinct anomalocaris
name: Anomalocaris
real: yes
says: a fast Cambrian sea hunter with grasping front arms and sharp eyes

@extinct trilobites
name: Trilobites
real: yes
says: armored sea arthropods that lived for nearly 300 million years, ended by the Great Dying

@extinct sea-scorpions
name: Sea scorpions (eurypterids)
real: yes
says: giant sea and river hunters; Jaekelopterus grew over 2.5 m long

@extinct ammonites
name: Ammonites
real: yes
says: coiled-shell relatives of squid, everywhere in the seas until the dinosaurs' end

# ── Early fish and the walk onto land ──

@extinct placoderms
name: Placoderms
real: yes
says: armored fish with bony plates for jaws
example: Dunkleosteus, an armored hunter up to about 10 m long

@extinct tiktaalik
name: Tiktaalik
real: yes
says: a fish with a neck and leg-like fins, halfway onto land

@extinct giant-insects
name: Giant insects
real: yes
says: oxygen-rich Carboniferous air let insects grow huge
example: Meganeura, a dragonfly-like hunter with wings about 70 cm across

@extinct arthropleura
name: Arthropleura
real: yes
says: a millipede relative up to about 3 m long, a plant eater

@extinct dimetrodon
name: Dimetrodon
real: yes
says: a sail-backed hunter, closer to mammals than to dinosaurs

# ── Dinosaurs ──

@dinosaur theropods
name: Theropods
real: yes
says: two-legged meat-eaters, and the line that became birds
example: Tyrannosaurus, Velociraptor, Spinosaurus, Allosaurus

@dinosaur sauropods
name: Sauropods
real: yes
says: huge long-necked plant-eaters, the largest land animals ever
example: Brachiosaurus, Diplodocus, Argentinosaurus

@dinosaur ornithopods
name: Ornithopods
real: yes
says: beaked plant-eaters, many duck-billed
example: Iguanodon, Parasaurolophus

@dinosaur ceratopsians
name: Horned dinosaurs (ceratopsians)
real: yes
example: Triceratops

@dinosaur stegosaurs
name: Plated dinosaurs (stegosaurs)
real: yes
example: Stegosaurus

@dinosaur ankylosaurs
name: Armored dinosaurs (ankylosaurs)
real: yes
example: Ankylosaurus, with a club tail

@dinosaur pachycephalosaurs
name: Dome-headed dinosaurs
real: yes
example: Pachycephalosaurus

@dinosaur feathered
name: Feathered dinosaurs
real: yes
says: many dinosaurs had feathers long before flight
example: Archaeopteryx, between dinosaur and bird

@dinosaur birds-survive
name: Birds
real: yes
says: the one dinosaur line that survived; every bird alive is a dinosaur

# ── Other Mesozoic giants ──

@extinct pterosaurs
name: Pterosaurs
real: yes
says: flying reptiles, not dinosaurs; some as big as small planes
example: Quetzalcoatlus, Pteranodon

@extinct ichthyosaurs
name: Ichthyosaurs
real: yes
says: dolphin-shaped sea reptiles

@extinct plesiosaurs
name: Plesiosaurs
real: yes
says: long-necked, four-flippered sea reptiles

@extinct mosasaurs
name: Mosasaurs
real: yes
says: giant sea lizards, top hunters of the last dinosaur seas

# ── After the dinosaurs: the age of mammals ──

@extinct megalodon
name: Megalodon
real: yes
says: a giant shark, far bigger than any shark alive

@extinct terror-birds
name: Terror birds
real: yes
says: tall flightless hunting birds

@extinct paraceratherium
name: Paraceratherium
real: yes
says: a hornless rhino relative, one of the largest land mammals ever

@extinct mammoth
name: Woolly mammoth
real: yes
says: ice-age elephant covered in fur

@extinct woolly-rhino
name: Woolly rhinoceros
real: yes

@extinct saber-tooth
name: Saber-toothed cats
real: yes
example: Smilodon

@extinct ground-sloth
name: Giant ground sloths
real: yes
says: sloths the size of elephants

@extinct short-faced-bear
name: Short-faced bear
real: yes

@extinct gigantopithecus
name: Gigantopithecus
real: yes
says: the largest ape ever

@extinct moa
name: Moa
real: yes
says: giant flightless birds, hunted out by humans

@extinct dodo
name: Dodo
real: yes
says: a flightless pigeon, gone soon after humans arrived

@extinct passenger-pigeon
name: Passenger pigeon
real: yes
says: once in flocks of billions, hunted out

@extinct thylacine
name: Thylacine
real: yes
says: a striped pouched hunter, gone in the 20th century

# ── Extinct plants ──

@extinctplant scale-trees
name: Scale trees (Lepidodendron)
real: yes
says: giant club-moss trees of the coal swamps; much of the world's coal is them

@extinctplant archaeopteris
name: Archaeopteris
real: yes
says: one of the first true trees

@extinctplant seed-ferns
name: Seed ferns
real: yes
says: fern-like plants that made seeds

@extinctplant glossopteris
name: Glossopteris
real: yes
says: a seed plant once across the southern supercontinent, ended by the Great Dying

# ── Generator rules ──

@rule extinct-seeds
real: rule
says: extinct real life is seed data: on Earth-like worlds, evolution can produce dinosaur-like, trilobite-like or mammoth-like life again, in new forms

@rule extinct-forever
real: rule
says: once a line dies out it never returns as the same line; it stays greyed out on the Tree of Life

@rule extinct-triggers
real: rule
says: mass extinctions follow real causes: impacts, supervolcanoes, warming, cooling, oxygen loss, and thinking species

@rule extinct-recovery
real: rule
says: after a mass extinction, survivors spread fast into the emptied world and new groups rise

@rule extinct-fossils
real: rule
says: extinct life leaves fossils; thinking species can dig them up and learn from them
